# One perspective triangle (test_lod.c's floor, its near half; 2-cycle, PERSP, TEX_LOD, six levels) with its LOD
# fraction drawn as the colour. The oracle divides the 16-bit integer halves of S, T and W with the console's
# reciprocal table; the model divides S >> 4 by all of W with its own reciprocal: S and T at the three points
# differ by a few subtexels, and with them the fraction (and near a power of two, the level). No texture is read.
# (The scissor stops at row 228: below it the triangle's right edge is past 2048 pixels, a difference of its own.)
rdram zero
cmd 3f10013f 00100000
cmd 2d000000 00500390
cmd 2f190cf0 00000000
cmd 3c66e1ff 8ffffe38
cmd 0a280432 043200aa f7b24925 00000000 00b40000 000a0000 00c17da0 fff5c390 00b302c6 011e0000 00040000 00000000 3333872b b6140000 7ae10000 00000000 0059fffc 008f0000 002cfffc 008f0000 999add2f 5b0a0000 cccddd2f 5b0a0000
cmd 29000000 00000000
